  ],
  "resolved_items": [
    {
      "item": "direct judge requested adjudication",
      "resolution": "Independent review identifies one substantive source ambiguity, rather than a disputed Lean definition: whether the arbitrary-profile solution assertion includes nondifferentiable profiles. The supplied evidence does not authorize silently selecting a classical restriction.",
      "primary_evidence": "Printed page 1, equations (1.2)–(1.3), defines partial-derivative notation but permits any profile function. The target guards its solution assertion with Differentiable Real profile."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge requested adjudication",
      "resolution": "The blind translation correctly reconstructs the supplied elaborated proposition. Its restricted PDE coverage originates in the target, not in a translation omission.",
      "primary_evidence": "Both dossiers place the differentiability implication inside the second conjunct. D001–D003 expand to exactly the translated construction and pointwise derivative requirements."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge classification is undetermined",
      "resolution": "Retain undetermined. Equivalence is supported for an explicitly selected classical reading; full arbitrary-profile solution coverage is not established. No evidence supports faithful-stronger.",
      "primary_evidence": "Printed page 1 does not qualify the profile's regularity. Methodology sections 2 and 9 prohibit treating restricted applicability or a silently corrected source statement as genuine strength."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge classification is undetermined",
      "resolution": "Retain undetermined on primary evidence, independently of agreement between judges. The accurately reconstructed target does not resolve the source's unspecified solution notion.",
      "primary_evidence": "The blind proposition requires everywhere differentiability only for the PDE conclusion. Printed page 2 repeats the traveling-profile interpretation for the opposite propagation direction without resolving nonsmooth solution semantics."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left dependency_coverage item D001 unclear",
      "resolution": "D001's meaning is resolved: it universally requires D003 at every real space-time pair. Its global domain matches the source; uncertainty concerns the source's solution class, not this quantifier.",
      "primary_evidence": "D001 body is ∀ (x t : Real), IsLinearAdvectionSolutionAt q speed x t. Printed page 1 supplies q on R × R."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left dependency_coverage item D003 unclear",
      "resolution": "D003's meaning is resolved: both ordinary slice derivatives must exist at the specified point and their values must satisfy qt + speed*qx = 0. It contains no generalized-solution alternative.",
      "primary_evidence": "D003 explicitly conjoins two HasDerivAt certificates and the residual equality. D014–D015 and the scalar-action projections specialize the action to real multiplication."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left dependency_coverage item D007 unclear",
      "resolution": "D007 requires differentiability at every real argument, without continuity of the derivative. This condition affects only PDE applicability. For this constructed field and D001's solution notion, it is also necessary: the spatial slice at t = 0 equals the profile.",
      "primary_evidence": "D007 unfolds to ∀ x, DifferentiableAt Real profile x. D002 gives travelingWave profile speed x 0 = profile x; D001 and D003 require that spatial slice to have a derivative at every x."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left dependency_coverage item D051 unclear",
      "resolution": "D051 requires actual ordinary point derivatives in the standard real topology. Rechecking its supplied body and current slice arguments confirms that neither default derivative values nor almost-everywhere derivatives can satisfy the requirement in their place.",
      "primary_evidence": "D051 uses HasDerivAtFilter with nhds x and the fixed base point. D003 applies it separately to temporal and spatial slices; the explicit real metric is |x-y|."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left semantic_checklist item C04 unclear",
      "resolution": "The hypothesis difference is established: global differentiability is explicit in Lean and absent from the printed wording. It is exactly appropriate for the target's solution predicate, but its status as an inherited source restriction remains unestablished.",
      "primary_evidence": "Printed page 1 states the profile is arbitrary. The target's second conjunct has antecedent Differentiable Real profile; D001–D003 require global slice differentiability."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left semantic_checklist item C05 unclear",
      "resolution": "The formula and unchanged-shape conclusion are fully represented for all profiles. The solution conclusion is complete for differentiable profiles only; no conclusion about nonsmooth PDE solutions is supplied.",
      "primary_evidence": "D002 is profile (x-speed*t), and the first conjunct states q(x+speed*t,t)=profile x without assumptions. The second conjunct is conditional."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left semantic_checklist item C07 unclear",
      "resolution": "Exact equality and the PDE signs match. Conditionalizing the solution claim cannot be counted as stronger. Whether it is equivalent or loses intended cases depends on the unresolved source interpretation.",
      "primary_evidence": "Equations (1.2)–(1.3) and D002–D003 have identical coefficient, subtraction, addition, and zero. The differentiability antecedent appears only in Lean."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left semantic_checklist item C10 unclear",
      "resolution": "There is no scalar, dimensional, velocity, or space-time specialization. The effective PDE domain is precisely everywhere differentiable real profiles; this is a restriction relative to a broader nonsmooth solution family.",
      "primary_evidence": "The elaborated target fixes E = Real, quantifies every real speed, and D001 quantifies every real x,t. D007 supplies the only profile restriction."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left semantic_checklist item C11 unclear",
      "resolution": "Zero and negative velocities and all real times are retained. Nondifferentiable profiles retain shape preservation but receive no PDE guarantee. Zero velocity does not eliminate D003's spatial derivative requirement.",
      "primary_evidence": "For profile ξ = |ξ|, D002 at t = 0 gives the spatial slice |x|, which has unequal one-sided difference quotients at zero. D003 requires its derivative even when speed = 0."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left semantic_checklist item N06 unclear",
      "resolution": "The constructed-family scope and absence of uniqueness match. Global differentiability is necessary and sufficient for this field to satisfy the stated global classical predicate, but the source does not explicitly identify that predicate as its complete solution notion.",
      "primary_evidence": "The source says the equation admits the displayed family. D001–D003 require derivative witnesses; the spatial slice at t = 0 gives necessity, and the chain rule gives sufficiency."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C04 unclear",
      "resolution": "The translated differentiability antecedent faithfully reflects Lean. Its absence from the printed source remains a source-scope question, not a blind-translation defect.",
      "primary_evidence": "The blind dossier's second conjunct contains Differentiable Real profile → LocalDef001; printed page 1 supplies no corresponding qualification."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C05 unclear",
      "resolution": "The translation includes both target conjuncts completely. It cannot recover an arbitrary-profile PDE conclusion because the target itself provides only conditional classical solvability.",
      "primary_evidence": "LocalDef002 defines the full profile formula; LocalDef001 and LocalDef003 supply the conditional derivative assertion. The first conjunct is unconditional."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C07 unclear",
      "resolution": "The translation preserves exact relation strength and logical scope. The remaining comparison uncertainty is whether the source intended more solution cases than the target covers.",
      "primary_evidence": "The blind elaborated type uses And, Eq, and a differentiability implication in exactly the same positions as the direct elaborated type."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C10 unclear",
      "resolution": "The translation correctly reports all real profiles as outer binders while distinguishing the smaller class receiving a PDE guarantee. Outer universal quantification does not remove that effective restriction.",
      "primary_evidence": "Both elaborated types universally quantify profile and speed, then condition only the solution conjunct on D007."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C11 unclear",
      "resolution": "The translated exceptional-case analysis is correct. The absolute-value profile demonstrates the lack of a classical derivative guarantee without contradicting either target conjunct; it does not determine the source's intended generalized interpretation.",
      "primary_evidence": "D002 preserves translated absolute-value profiles algebraically. D007 fails at their original corner, and D003 requires an actual spatial derivative."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item N06 unclear",
      "resolution": "The translation introduces no uniqueness or converse representation theorem. Its classical regularity restriction is exact for the Lean predicate, while correspondence to the complete source solution family remains unresolved.",
      "primary_evidence": "LocalDef001–LocalDef003 concern only the explicitly constructed field and derivative witnesses. Printed page 1 asserts a solution family rather than an exhaustive classification."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left implication lean_implies_source unclear",
      "resolution": "The reverse comparison remains unclear for the full selected source claim. Lean establishes the unrestricted geometric claim and the classical differentiable subcase, but does not establish a nonsmooth solution assertion. Selecting an implicit classical reading would settle this direction positively only under that additional interpretive choice.",
      "primary_evidence": "The target's two conjuncts and D001–D003 show its exact coverage. Printed pages 1–2 do not supply the missing regularity or generalized-solution convention."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left implication translation_implies_source unclear",
      "resolution": "The same uncertainty remains after verifying the translation against the declarations. It is not resolved by either judge's agreement or by dependency reuse hashes.",
      "primary_evidence": "The blind and direct dossiers agree after replacing LocalDef001–LocalDef004 with their corresponding direct names; the authoritative passage retains its unqualified arbitrary-profile wording."
    },
    {
      "item": "Nonvacuity and purported stronger content",
      "resolution": "The theorem is substantively nonvacuous. For profile ξ = ξ and speed = 1, q(x,t)=x-t has qt=-1 and qx=1 everywhere. The unconditional transport identity is the source's shape-preservation assertion expressed algebraically, not an additional strengthening that compensates for reduced PDE applicability.",
      "primary_evidence": "D002 yields x-t in this example; D003 requires genuine derivative witnesses with -1+1=0. The sentence following (1.3) explicitly asserts unchanged shape."
    }
  ],
  "implications": {
    "lean_implies_source": {
      "verdict": "unclear",
      "reasoning": "Unfolding D002 gives exactly q(x,t)=profile(x-speed*t), and the unconditional first conjunct gives unchanged propagation for every profile. D001–D003 supply the source PDE everywhere when the profile is everywhere differentiable. This covers the full claim under an implicit classical-admissibility reading, since at t=0 the spatial derivative requirement already forces profile differentiability. However, the printed passage permits any function without specifying that restriction or a generalized solution notion. The theorem makes no nonsmooth PDE assertion. The supplied primary context therefore does not establish that its coverage exhausts the selected source claim."
    },
    "source_implies_lean": {
      "verdict": "yes",
      "reasoning": "The source formula implies q(x+speed*t,t)=profile x by real arithmetic. On the everywhere differentiable subcase explicitly assumed in Lean, the same formula gives qx=profile'(x-speed*t) and qt=-speed*profile'(x-speed*t) by ordinary differentiation. These are actual derivative witnesses satisfying qt+speed*qx=0 at every real pair, exactly as D001–D003 require. This consequence uses the formula and the added antecedent directly and does not rely on treating an unqualified arbitrary-profile classical assertion as a valid premise."
    }
  },
  "classification": "undetermined",
  "accepted": false,
  "remaining_uncertainties": [
    "The supplied primary passage and adjacent page do not determine whether the arbitrary-profile solution assertion implicitly restricts classical admissibility or includes nonsmooth solutions under an unstated generalized interpretation.",
    "If a generalized interpretation is intended, its admissible profile class and precise solution notion are unspecified. Arbitrary real functions cannot simply be presumed to define ordinary distributional solutions without further conditions.",
    "Primary-source inspection used the supplied page renderings. The PDF bytes and supplied provenance hashes were not independently recomputed."
  ],
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "category": "unresolved-source-solution-scope",
      "evidence": "Printed page 1 combines partial-derivative notation with an arbitrary-profile solution assertion. Lean explicitly restricts the PDE guarantee through Differentiable Real profile and requires actual derivatives through D001, D003, and D051.",
      "impact": "The target is a precise nonvacuous classical formulation, but acceptance as the complete selected source result requires resolving the source interpretation. Restricted applicability cannot justify faithful-stronger."
    },
    {
      "severity": "note",
      "category": "classical-regularity-is-exact-for-target",
      "evidence": "At t=0, D002's spatial slice is the profile itself, so D001–D003 imply everywhere profile differentiability. Conversely, differentiability supplies both required slice derivatives by the chain rule.",
      "impact": "The antecedent is not excessive relative to the chosen global classical predicate. This resolves the Lean-side regularity question without establishing that the source chose the same solution class."
    },
    {
      "severity": "note",
      "category": "unconditional-propagation-preserved",
      "evidence": "D002 defines the exact source formula, and the first conjunct asserts q(x+speed*t,t)=profile x for all profiles, real speeds, and real space-time points.",
      "impact": "The geometric propagation claim is fully represented, including nonsmooth profiles and zero or negative velocities."
    }
  ],
  "rationale": "The supplied declaration bodies resolve every disputed dependency's mathematical meaning: global quantification, exact translation, ordinary derivative existence, and everywhere differentiability. The explicit structures preserve real arithmetic, topology, scalar multiplication, and witness dependence; the reuse ledger establishes provenance rather than source equivalence. The blind translation accurately reflects these declarations. The source renderings establish the formula and propagation claim but do not resolve the solution interpretation of arbitrary profiles. Consequently, source-to-Lean follows for the stated differentiable subcase, while Lean-to-source remains unclear for the complete selected claim. Under the supplied classification policy, undetermined with accepted=false preserves that uncertainty without misclassifying a restricted classical formulation as stronger."
}
